  "_tarotNote": "Tarot correspondences follow the Rider-Waite-Smith (RWS) system and the standard numerology-to-Major-Arcana mapping used in mainstream Western esoteric tradition: 1 The Magician, 2 The High Priestess, 3 The Empress, 4 The Emperor, 5 The Hierophant, 6 The Lovers, 7 The Chariot, 8 Strength (RWS numbering, where Strength is VIII and Justice is XI), 9 The Hermit. For the master numbers we use the card whose Major Arcana number matches directly: 11 Justice (XI), 22 The World (XXII, the twenty-second and final trump when The Fool is counted as 0 through 21 plus its own hidden 22nd station), and 33 has no single canonical trump, so we assign The Sun (XIX, which reduces 1+9 to 10 to 1) as its resonant 'master teacher' card by tradition; The Fool (0) is noted as the ungrounded potential behind all master numbers. Planetary, elemental, chakra and color attributions blend Pythagorean numerology with the Hermetic/Golden Dawn correspondences.",
